    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "t_start": 0.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.0,
      "narration_text": "Konnichiwa. This is Liam, in for Bear. What if you never had to type a long prompt again? What if Claude already knew everything about you — before the first word? The files are the prompt. Let me show you.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "COMPOSER_ASK",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "type",
        "scene_type": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "ask": "Write a LinkedIn post in my voice.",
            "answer_preview": "Claude already knows your tone, your rules, your goals — because it read your files first.",
            "command": "What if you never had to type a long prompt again?",
            "greeting": "Konnichiwa. This is Liam"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[COMPOSER] cold open ask + Liam sign-in",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-10T03:51:22"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 10.67,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "t_start": 9.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.0,
      "narration_text": "Claude Cowork connects to a folder on your computer. You save text files in that folder — your style, your rules, your goals. Claude reads them automatically before every session. The files are the prompt. Forever. No more 500-word instruction blocks every time you start a chat.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "hold",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CoworkComposer",
          "props": {
            "typedText": "Always read about-me, leave the rest alone",
            "heading": "Files are the prompt.",
            "subline": "Save style, rules, and goals as .md files. Claude reads them before every session.",
            "chips": {
              "scope": "Work",
              "mode": "Research"
            }
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "card": {
        "kind": "spark",
        "eyebrow": "CLAUDE COWORK",
        "copy": "Files are the prompt.",
        "sub": "Save your style, rules, and goals as .md files. Claude reads them before every session — automatically.",
        "accent": "#D97757"
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[SPARK] Cowork core concept",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-10T03:51:22"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 15.13,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "t_start": 18.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.0,
      "narration_text": "The Cowork folder structure: three subfolders. About-me — three files: about-me, anti-ai-writing-style, my-company. Claude-output — you never touch this; it's where Claude stores its work. Templates — you never touch this either; it's where your favourite work formats live. Set up Global Instructions to tell Claude: always read about-me, leave the rest alone.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CoworkSideRail",
          "props": {
            "folders": [
              {
                "label": "Claude Cowork",
                "depth": 0,
                "open": true
              },
              {
                "label": "about-me",
                "depth": 1,
                "open": true,
                "hi": true
              },
              {
                "label": "about-me.md",
                "depth": 2,
                "fileMeta": "edit me"
              },
              {
                "label": "anti-ai-writing-style.md",
                "depth": 2
              },
              {
                "label": "my-company.md",
                "depth": 2
              },
              {
                "label": "claude-output",
                "depth": 1,
                "open": false
              },
              {
                "label": "templates",
                "depth": 1,
                "open": false
              }
            ],
            "contextNote": "Global Instructions: always read about-me"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "illustration": {
        "concept": "Claude Cowork folder tree with three subfolders and their contents",
        "layout": "Vertical folder tree. Root: Claude Cowork. Branch 1: about-me (3 child files). Branch 2: claude-output (label: do not touch). Branch 3: templates (label: do not touch). Global Instructions node at bottom with arrow from about-me."
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[ILLUSTRATION] Cowork folder structure",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-10T03:51:22"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 18.56,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "t_start": 28.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.0,
      "narration_text": "The problem: managing .md files is genuinely annoying. You double-click one, it opens a geeky text editor full of hashtags and asterisks. Hard to read. Hard to edit. Most people set up Cowork once, then never touch their files again. So the context goes stale.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "hold",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CoworkTaskView",
          "props": {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "prompt",
                "text": "Open about-me.md"
              },
              {
                "type": "toolline",
                "text": "Opens a text editor full of hashtags and asterisks",
                "spinner": false
              },
              {
                "type": "review",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "title": "Hard to read — raw markdown",
                    "badge": "Problem",
                    "badgeTone": "warn"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Hard to edit — most skip updates",
                    "badge": "Problem",
                    "badgeTone": "warn"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Context goes stale → generic output",
                    "badge": "Problem",
                    "badgeTone": "fail"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "cues": [
              0,
              18,
              35
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "card": {
        "kind": "spark",
        "eyebrow": "CLAUDE COWORK",
        "copy": "The files go stale.",
        "sub": "Raw .md files are hard to edit. Most people never update them. Stale context = generic output.",
        "accent": "#D97757"
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[SPARK] the stale-context problem",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-10T03:51:22"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 14.76,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "t_start": 37.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.0,
      "narration_text": "The fix is Obsidian. It's free. You point it at your Cowork folder and it turns every file into a beautifully rendered document — headers, bold, bullet points. A sidebar to navigate. Search across everything. You click a file, edit it right there. It saves back to the same folder Cowork reads. One edit in Obsidian, Claude knows instantly.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "hold",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CoworkComposer",
          "props": {
            "typedText": "Open folder as vault → point at Cowork folder",
            "heading": "Obsidian. It's free.",
            "subline": "Every .md file becomes a clean, editable doc. Edit → Claude knows immediately.",
            "hint": "One edit in Obsidian, Claude knows instantly."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "card": {
        "kind": "spark",
        "eyebrow": "CLAUDE COWORK",
        "copy": "Obsidian. It's free.",
        "sub": "Point it at your Cowork folder. Every .md file becomes a clean, editable doc. Edit → Claude knows immediately.",
        "accent": "#D97757"
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[SPARK] Obsidian as the fix",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-10T03:51:22"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 18.24,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "t_start": 47.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 12.0,
      "narration_text": "Why Obsidian and not the others? Notion: cloud-based, stores everything in its own database, you'd have to re-import every time Cowork updates a file. Google Docs: not .md files, constant conversion back and forth. VS Code: for developers. GitHub: requires git, commits, pushes. Obsidian wins because it reads your existing folder directly. No import. No sync. No hidden metadata injected. Your .md files stay exactly as Cowork expects them.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CoworkTaskView",
          "props": {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "section",
                "text": "Why Obsidian wins"
              },
              {
                "type": "review",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "title": "Notion",
                    "badge": "Cloud DB — re-import every time",
                    "badgeTone": "fail"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Google Docs",
                    "badge": "Not .md — constant conversion",
                    "badgeTone": "fail"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "VS Code",
                    "badge": "For developers",
                    "badgeTone": "warn"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "GitHub",
                    "badge": "Requires git commits",
                    "badgeTone": "warn"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Obsidian",
                    "badge": "Reads folder directly — no import",
                    "badgeTone": "pass"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "cues": [
              0,
              10,
              22,
              34,
              46,
              60
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "illustration": {
        "concept": "Tool comparison: why each alternative fails vs why Obsidian wins",
        "layout": "Two columns. Left: rejected tools (Notion, Google Docs, VS Code, GitHub) each with a one-line failure reason and an X. Right: Obsidian with a check and three win reasons. Draw-in left column first, then right."
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[ILLUSTRATION] Obsidian vs alternatives comparison",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-10T03:51:22"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 23.82,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "t_start": 59.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.0,
      "narration_text": "The daily workflow is two apps, one folder. Open Obsidian to browse, search, read, and edit your files. Open Cowork to build new work and generate outputs. Both look at the same folder. Always in sync. Obsidian is where you update the brain. Cowork is where you build. You can also add a Skills folder — one file per repeated task, each callable with a slash command.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "hold",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CoworkTaskView",
          "props": {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "section",
                "text": "Two apps. One folder."
              },
              {
                "type": "toolline",
                "text": "Obsidian — update the brain (browse, search, edit)",
                "spinner": false
              },
              {
                "type": "toolline",
                "text": "Cowork — build (generate, output)",
                "spinner": false
              },
              {
                "type": "toolline",
                "text": "Same folder. Always in sync.",
                "spinner": false
              },
              {
                "type": "toolline",
                "text": "Skills subfolder → slash-command workflows",
                "spinner": false
              }
            ],
            "cues": [
              0,
              14,
              28,
              40,
              52
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B07.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "card": {
        "kind": "spark",
        "eyebrow": "CLAUDE COWORK",
        "copy": "Two apps. One folder.",
        "sub": "Obsidian = update the brain. Cowork = build. Same folder, always in sync. Add a Skills subfolder for slash-command workflows.",
        "accent": "#D97757"
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[SPARK] daily two-app workflow",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-10T03:51:22"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 19.22,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "t_start": 69.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.0,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. Download Obsidian from obsidian.md — it's free. Click 'Open folder as a vault.' Point it at your Cowork folder. Open your about-me file. Change one line. Open a new Cowork session. Watch Claude reflect the change.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "hold",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CoworkComposer",
          "props": {
            "typedText": "Open folder as vault → point at Cowork → change one line in about-me",
            "heading": "Your turn. Download Obsidian.",
            "subline": "obsidian.md — free. Open folder as vault. Watch the change land in Cowork.",
            "hint": "Change one line in about-me. Open Cowork. Watch Claude reflect the change."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B08.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "card": {
        "kind": "handoff",
